[ti:(untitled)]
[ar:VESAHE · hkfaduio]
[al:Cinematic & Other]
[by:Radio Vaigyaaniq — draft timing, unverified]
[00:08.00]मच्छर-पंडित संवाद
[00:11.17]Machchar-Pandit Sammwad
[00:14.34]A Conversation Between a Mosquito and a Scholar
[00:17.50]प्रस्तावना Prastāvanā (Introduction)
[00:20.67]A pandit, steeped in the Vedas, sits by the river at dusk, reciting the great mahāvākyas:
[00:23.84]aham brahmasmi … aham dwaitam … aham advaitam … vayam sādhanā asti …
[00:27.01]A mosquito lands on his forearm.
[00:30.18]What follows is not a debate. It is a sammwad—a living dialogue between philosophy and life, between the seeker of stillness and the necessity of hunger, between aham (I) and vayam (we).
[00:33.34]भाग १: प्रथम भेंट Bhāg 1: Pratham Bheṇṭ (First Meeting)
[00:36.51]Machchar (buzzing softly):
[00:39.68]अहम् … अहम् …
[00:42.85]Aham … aham …
[00:46.02]You keep saying I, I.
[00:49.18]But this I — does it itch?
[00:52.35]Pandit (startled):
[00:55.52]You are but a mosquito. I am a knower of Brahman.
[00:58.69]I speak of the Self — the ātman — not this itching skin.
[01:01.86]Machchar:
[01:05.02]Then why did you flinch?
[01:08.19]When I touched you, some I moved.
[01:11.36]Was that Brahman flinching?
[01:14.53]Or was it just you — the one who doesn't want to be touched by me?
[01:17.70]Pandit (irritated):
[01:20.86]You disturb my meditation.
[01:24.03]I am contemplating non-duality — advaita.
[01:27.20]There is no separate you, no separate me.
[01:30.37]We are one.
[01:33.54]Machchar:
[01:36.70]If we are one,
[01:39.87]then when I drink a drop of your blood,
[01:43.04]am I not simply offering ahuti (oblation) to the Self?
[01:46.21]Why do you call it disturbance?
[01:49.38]Why do you raise your hand to strike me?
[01:52.54]Pandit (hand frozen mid-air):
[01:55.71]…
[01:58.88]Machchar:
[02:02.05]You chant vayam sādhanā asti —
[02:05.22]We are the practice.
[02:08.38]But your practice excludes me.
[02:11.55]Your we is only other pandits, other men, other ahams like yours.
[02:14.72]Pandit (slowly lowering hand):
[02:17.89]What do you want, mosquito?
[02:21.06]Machchar:
[02:24.22]Nothing.
[02:27.39]I am already what you are seeking.
[02:30.56]I am the itch in your meditation.
[02:33.73]I am the fragment that breaks your aham brahmasmi into
[02:36.90]aham … aham … aham …
[02:40.06]until you hear not your own voice,
[02:43.23]but the buzzing of the One who speaks through all mouths —
[02:46.40]even this tiny one.
[02:49.57]Pandit (after a long silence):
[02:52.74]Then teach me.
[02:55.90]Machchar:
[02:59.07]I already have.
[03:02.24]You were reciting aham dwaitam, aham advaitam.
[03:05.41]I came as dwaita — the other, the irritant, the small.
[03:08.58]But if you do not kill me,
[03:11.74]you may find I am also advaita —
[03:14.91]the one who makes your aham real
[03:18.08]by being the not-aham that you nevertheless cannot separate from.
[03:21.25]Pandit:
[03:24.42]What is the mantra, then?
[03:27.58]Machchar:
[03:30.75]No mantra.
[03:33.92]Just sit here.
[03:37.09]Let me land.
[03:40.26]Do not flinch.
[03:43.42]Do not kill.
[03:46.59]Let the I that itches and the I that recites
[03:49.76]become one buzz.
[03:52.93]That is vayam.
[03:56.10]Pandit closes his eyes. The mosquito lands again. He does not move.
[03:59.26]Machchar (whispering, or perhaps it is the wind):
[04:02.43]vayam sādhanā asti …
[04:05.60]We are the practice.
[04:08.77]Even this.
[04:11.94]Especially this.
[04:15.10]भाग २: पंडित का विलाप Bhāg 2: Paṇḍit kā Vilāp (The Scholar's Lament)
[04:18.27]दीमी दीमी हम्मmmmmm
[04:21.44]हाय रे मच्छरी तेरी याद आवे है
[04:24.61]Dhīmī dhīmī hmmmmm
[04:27.78]haye re machchharī terī yād āve hai
[04:30.94]Softly, softly… hmmmmm
[04:34.11]Oh, mosquito, your memory comes to me
[04:37.28]Where are you now,
[04:40.45]you who landed on my forearm
[04:43.62]and turned my aham brahmasmi
[04:46.78]into a question mark?
[04:49.95]Your buzz was my first mantra.
[04:53.12]Your itch was my first sparsha (touch)
[04:56.29]that was not mine to control.
[04:59.46]उ पंडित अपने भला कहा
[05:02.62]दुनिया ने झूठ बहकावे है
[05:05.79]U paṇḍit apne bhalā kahā
[05:08.96]duniyā ne jhūṭh bahakāve hai
[05:12.13]That pandit—where is his goodness now?
[05:15.30]The world has deceived him with false lures
[05:18.46]I sat on my āsana,
[05:21.63]wrapped in my shawl of jñāna,
[05:24.80]and called it wisdom.
[05:27.97]But the world—
[05:31.14]the world with its mango blossoms,
[05:34.30]its river at dusk,
[05:37.47]its tiny mosquito—
[05:40.64]whispered a different truth:
[05:43.81]Wisdom that cannot welcome a mosquito
[05:46.98]is not wisdom.
[05:50.14]It is just another fortress.
[05:53.31]You came to me as dwaita—
[05:56.48]the other, the small, the nuisance.
[05:59.65]I wanted advaita—
[06:02.82]the grand, the silent, the undisturbed.
[06:05.98]But you said:
[06:09.15]Let me land. Do not kill. Let the I that itches
[06:12.32]and the I that recites become one buzz.
[06:15.49]And in that moment,
[06:18.66]advaita was not a philosophy.
[06:21.82]It was a mosquito on my skin,
[06:24.99]and my hand not moving.
[06:28.16]Now I sit by the same river.
[06:31.33]I chant vayam sādhanā asti.
[06:34.50]But the we feels incomplete without you.
[06:37.66]दीमी दीमी हम्मmmmmm
[06:40.83]हाय रे मच्छरी तेरी याद आवे है
[06:44.00]Come back, little one.
[06:47.17]Land on me again.
[06:50.34]Let me remember
[06:53.50]that the anthem is not in my chanting alone—
[06:56.67]it is in the buzz I once called disturbance.
